    "created_at": "2023-01-30T17:25:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-30T17:25:21Z",
    "body": "> I'd expect two different requests if there's a microtask checkpoint after the src assignment but before the base change.\r\n\r\nWhy would changing a document's base URL _after_ an image's microtask checkpoint has already been run somehow refetch that image, and re-resolve its URL?\r\n\r\n1. Microtask checkpoint reached; image request is made\r\n2. Document's base URL is manipulated\r\n3. Image is inserted into DOM — I don't think this should cause a re-fetch due to the document base URL changing from the last time the image is fetched; refetching would mean counting insertion as a \"relevant mutation\" and keeping track of the old state of the base URL, I think",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1409024335/reactions",
