    "body": "> That's right. If you change src with srcset, then should it run? If we define the URL comparison on the parsed / resolved URI, then it should, but otherwise it should not.\r\n\r\nYep that makes sense to me; if you changed src/srcset _or_ if we defined the URL comparison (that takes place in step 5 of [#reacting-to-environment-changes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#reacting-to-environment-changes)) to not be relative, then it seems the image would be refetched upon insertion if the Document's base URL has changed. Do you think there is any appetite to do this? Do browser disagree on this case currently?\r\n\r\nIf not, since my CL with the test has landed, I'm happy to file a couple browser bugs and close this issue.",
